            <ArticleTitle>Complete Genome Sequence of a Shiga Toxin-Producing Enterobacter cloacae Clinical Isolate.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e00883-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.00883-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Enterobacter cloacae strain M12X01451 was isolated from a patient with mild diarrhea. This strain produces a novel subtype of Shiga toxin 1, Stx1e. The Stx1e-converting prophage in strain M12X01451 is stable and can infect other bacteria following induction. Here we report the complete genome sequence and annotation of strain M12X01451.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
